                            <li><strong>Inflation (CPI):</strong> Higher inflation in ${fObj.country} typically weakens the ${f}.</li>
                            <li><strong>Trade Flows:</strong> Import/Export volumes between the two regions.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <div style="background:var(--input-bg); padding:20px; border-radius:8px; border-left:4px solid var(--accent); margin:20px 0;">
                            <strong>💡 Strategy:</strong> Check the <strong>1-Year Chart</strong> above. If the rate is near a 52-week high, it is historically a good time to convert ${f} to ${t}.
                        </div>

                        <h3>How to get the best rate?</h3>
                        <p>Avoid exchanging money at hotels or airports. Use online transfer services or local banks that offer rates close to the mid-market rate shown here.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            `;
        }

        document.getElementById('newsPopup').scrollTop = 0;
    }

